<<<
wicked:—Because the d.’s a. always starts with the advantage of possessing a bad case, Talleyrand’s defender calls forth all our chivalrous sympathy.
===
wicked:—*Because the d.'s a. always starts with the advantage of possessing a bad case, Talleyrand's defender calls forth all our chivalrous sympathy.*
